-- title:
--   Inertia-invariant n-torsion bounded by finite part times component group
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0\ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime with $p\nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$, meaning that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, and let $\Lambda$ be a level datum for $(N_0,p,A)$: a morphism $\sigma_A\colon \operatorname{Spec} A\to \mathrm{base}\,p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over $\mathrm{base}\,p$ with a relative group law, and bijections of $J_0(N_0)$ and of its characteristic-$p$ analogue over the residue field of $A$ with the sections of $X$ over the generic and the residual point. Assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian`, i.e. the bundle of abelian-scheme properties holds, the group law is commutative, both parametrisations are additive, the generic parametrisation is Galois-equivariant, reduction of points agrees modulo $\ell$ whenever the relevant inputs are present, and every Hecke operator is realised by an endomorphism over the base. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data and let $n>0$. Then the number of points of the intersection, inside $J_0(N_0p)$, of the $n$-torsion subgroup (the submodule killed by $n$) with the subgroup of elements fixed by the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ is at most the number of points of `O.finPts n` — the subgroup generated by the $n$-torsion points whose associated section extends to the place $A$ — times the order of $\operatorname{componentGroup}(O.\mathrm{width})$, the quotient of $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb Z}(\text{characterLattice},\mathbb Z)$ by the image of the Gram map of the width function of $O$.
--
--   This is the counted form of the Néron mapping property for inertia-invariant points: the invariant $n$-torsion is squeezed between the part extending over the place $A$ and the component group of the special fibre. It is one of the elementary steps in the proof that prime-to-$p$ toric torsion lies in the monodromy part, used in [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.toricPts_le_toricMonodromyPart_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_toricPts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.toricPts_le_toricMonodromyPart_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_toricPts).
